IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `imm-types`

-- Immigration Act 2009 — GOALS 1 AND 2: ELIGIBILITY, UNLAWFUL STATUS AND
-- WORK.
--
--   "May the person be granted a visa; are they unlawfully in New Zealand,
--    since when, and by when may they appeal or seek reconsideration?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2009_51.txt — ss 9, 15-17,
-- 21, 154, 185.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — eligibility, unlawful status and work`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- s 15 "(1) No visa or entry permission may be granted, and no visa waiver
-- may apply, to any person— (a) who, at any time ..., has been convicted of an
-- offence for which the person has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term
-- of 5 years or more, or for an indeterminate period capable of running for 5
-- years or more; or (b) who, at any time in the preceding 10 years ..., has
-- been convicted of an offence for which the person has been sentenced to
-- imprisonment for a term of 12 months or more ...; or (c) who is subject to a
-- period of prohibition on entry ...; or (d) who at any time ... has been
-- removed or deported from New Zealand ...; or (e) who is excluded ...; or (f)
-- who has, at any time, been removed, excluded, or deported from another
-- country." s 16: the Minister's reason to believe. s 17 "(1) Despite
-- sections 15 and 16, a visa and entry permission may be granted to any
-- person— (a) in accordance with a special direction; or (b) in accordance
-- with section 83." "The preceding 10 years" runs back from the day of the
-- decision, its anniversary included (fork F1).
@ref ss 15-17
@export Whether a person is barred from being granted a visa or entry permission on a day under ss 15-17 of the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ): ever sentenced to 5 years' imprisonment or more; convicted in the preceding 10 years with a sentence of 12 months or more; subject to a prohibition on entry; ever removed or deported from New Zealand (outside the s 15(3) exceptions), excluded, or removed, excluded or deported from another country; or the subject of the Minister's s 16 belief — unless a special direction or s 83 applies. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A Person  @desc Convictions and sentences, prohibition, deportation, exclusion, the Minister's belief, and any special direction
      d IS A DATE  @desc The day of the decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred from a visa` p `on` d IF
        NOT p's `a special direction or s 83 applies`
    AND (   any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `sentence of imprisonment, in years` AT LEAST 5) (p's `convictions`)
         OR any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `sentence of imprisonment, in years` AT LEAST 1 AND c's `convicted on` AT LEAST `add years` d (0 MINUS 10) AND c's `convicted on` AT MOST d) (p's `convictions`)
         OR p's `subject to a period of prohibition on entry`
         OR p's `removed or deported from New Zealand, outside the s 15(3) exceptions`
         OR p's `excluded from New Zealand under an enactment`
         OR p's `removed, excluded or deported from another country`
         OR p's `the Minister has a s 16 reason to believe`)

-- s 9 "(1) ... a person who is not a New Zealand citizen is unlawfully in New
-- Zealand if the person is in New Zealand but— (a) is not the holder of a visa
-- granted under this Act; or (b) has not been granted entry permission ...
-- (2) A person's status as being unlawfully in New Zealand is calculated— (a)
-- as starting on the date the person arrived in New Zealand, if the person
-- has never been lawfully in New Zealand since his or her arrival; or (b) as
-- starting on the day after the date on which the person's visa expired or
-- was cancelled without another visa being granted".
@ref s 9(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is unlawfully in New Zealand` p IF
        NOT p's `a New Zealand citizen`
    AND ((NOT p's `holds a visa`) OR (NOT p's `has been granted entry permission`))

@ref s 9(2)(a)-(b)
@export The day a person's unlawful status in New Zealand starts under s 9(2) of the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ): the day they arrived, if never lawfully in New Zealand since; otherwise the day after their visa expired or was cancelled without another being granted. Nothing if they are not unlawfully in New Zealand. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A Person  @desc Citizenship, visa and entry permission, arrival, and the last visa's expiry or cancellation
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day unlawful status starts for` p MEANS
    IF   NOT `is unlawfully in New Zealand` p
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   NOT p's `has been lawfully in New Zealand since arriving`
         THEN JUST (p's `arrived in New Zealand on`)
         ELSE CONSIDER p's `last visa expired or was cancelled on`
              WHEN JUST ended THEN JUST (`the day` 1 `days after` ended)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 9(2) needs the date the visa expired or was cancelled`

`s 9(2) needs the date the visa expired or was cancelled` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 9(2)(b): the person was lawful once, but no date of visa expiry or cancellation is given"

-- s 21 "A person who is unlawfully in New Zealand may not— (a) work in New
-- Zealand or in the exclusive economic zone".
@ref s 21(a)
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred from working by s 21` p IF
    `is unlawfully in New Zealand` p

-- s 154 "(2) A person unlawfully in New Zealand may, not later than 42 days
-- after first becoming unlawfully in New Zealand, appeal on humanitarian
-- grounds against his or her liability for deportation. ... (4) If the person
-- is unlawfully in New Zealand following an unsuccessful reconsideration
-- under section 185 ..., ... not later than 42 days after the later of— (a)
-- the day on which the person became unlawfully in New Zealand; or (b) the
-- day on which the person received confirmation of the decision".
@ref s 154(2), (4)
GIVEN became IS A DATE, confirmed IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a humanitarian appeal by a person unlawful from` became `, reconsideration confirmed` confirmed MEANS
    CONSIDER confirmed
    WHEN JUST c THEN `the day` 42 `days after` (IF c GREATER THAN became THEN c ELSE became)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day` 42 `days after` became

-- s 185 "(2) The applicant may apply ... for a reconsideration ... if, and
-- only if,— (a) the application for reconsideration is made not later than
-- 14 days after the date on which the applicant received notice of the
-- decision ...; and (b) the applicant is still lawfully in New Zealand at the
-- time of the application".
@ref s 185(2)
GIVEN notified IS A DATE, applied IS A DATE, lawful IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reconsideration may be applied for, notified` notified `, applying on` applied `, still lawful` lawful IF
        applied AT MOST `the day` 14 `days after` notified
    AND lawful
